WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.000
The workbook's books
already design most of this.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.186
Cloud Boundary and Landing
Zone builds the hierarchy,

3
00:00:06.186 --> 00:00:09.938
the boundary policies, the
provisioning loop and the ownership.

4
00:00:09.938 --> 00:00:14.000
Security Operations and Telemetry
chooses the posture tool.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.877
Network and Transport
owns the agency edge,

6
00:00:17.877 --> 00:00:21.862
and DNS, DHCP and IPAM
owns name resolution.

7
00:00:21.862 --> 00:00:27.038
What none of them gives is the service-by-service
engineering of the Azure controls

8
00:00:27.038 --> 00:00:31.088
a Zero Trust assessment tests: DDoS
protection on every public I P,

9
00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:35.963
a web application firewall in prevention
mode, origins only the edge can reach,

10
00:00:35.963 --> 00:00:40.988
egress through an inspecting firewall,
platform services reached only through

11
00:00:40.988 --> 00:00:45.713
private endpoints, and keys behind
role-based access with purge protection.

12
00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:50.315
Microsoft Learn's Azure network
security Zero Trust recommendations

13
00:00:50.315 --> 00:00:53.880
list those checks, and the
guide takes each one as a step.
